From 4f034f9f47921ee24760aad56307552a230c5794 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chatgptyukkuri <chatgptyukkuri@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:35:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zink: don't use extended dynamic state on the ARM proprietary
 driver

The Vulkan wrapper used by Winlator and GameNative on Mali hides
VK_EXT_extended_dynamic_state and VK_EXT_extended_dynamic_state2 from
everything but DXVK and vkd3d-proton because of driver bugs. Do the same
in zink. Disabling EDS1 also disables EDS2, EDS3, color write enable and
vertex input dynamic state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkAyMz3ChWUcwV1bWoNa1Z
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
index 7efcbaa0..6d2cfb8e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -2936,6 +2936,9 @@ init_driver_workarounds(struct zink_screen *screen)
    if (screen->info.props.limits.maxBoundDescriptorSets < ZINK_DESCRIPTOR_ALL_TYPES ||
        zink_debug & (ZINK_DEBUG_COMPACT | ZINK_DEBUG_NOSHOBJ))
       screen->info.have_EXT_shader_object = false;
+   if (zink_driverid(screen) == VK_DRIVER_ID_ARM_PROPRIETARY)
+      /* dynamic state is unreliable on the ARM proprietary driver */
+      screen->info.have_EXT_extended_dynamic_state = false;
    /* EDS2 is only used with EDS1 */
    if (!screen->info.have_EXT_extended_dynamic_state) {
       screen->info.have_EXT_extended_dynamic_state2 = false;
-- 
